"""
BOM AUTO-FILL TOOL  (Dunnes "New" tab BOM template)
=====================================================
Upload: BOM (.xlsx with a "New" tab), CBD costing (.xls/.xlsx), PO bundle (.pdf)
Output: a NEW workbook (your BOM is never changed) with
  - "New (Filled)"  : your New tab, columns A:T, filled/updated/flagged + helper columns U:X
  - "Change Log"    : every change with its source (PO no + PDF page, or CBD row)
  - "PO Lines"      : every PO line read from the PDF, and where it was used
  - "CBD Data"      : every CBD costing block (fabric + other costs, per dz and per pc)
  - "Checks"        : PO and CBD self-checks (totals). If anything here says FAIL, do not trust the run.

Cell colours in "New (Filled)":
  green  = blank filled from a PO
  peach  = filled from the CBD or inferred (not a printed PO price) -> confirm
  blue   = existing value replaced (placeholder like DTM, UOM, sourcing, split thread text). Old value in comment.
  orange = please check (BOM value disagrees with PO/CBD, or a judgment call). Value NOT changed.
  yellow (Item col) = BOM row with no PO found

Rules: it never guesses. A BOM row is filled only when exactly one PO item (or several identical ones) matches.
Ambiguous rows are reported, not filled.

Run (Colab):   from bom_tool import run;  run("BOM.xlsx", "CBD.xls", "PO.pdf")
Run (shell):   python bom_tool.py BOM.xlsx CBD.xls PO.pdf [--out OUT.xlsx] [--update] [--force]
